# Python bytecode caches.
#
# Added in Cycle 2 after a stale, *tracked* .pyc silently shadowed edited
# source for several minutes: Python skipped recompilation, so the module that
# ran was not the module on disk, and a passing/failing test could not be
# trusted either way. Bytecode is a build artifact of a specific interpreter
# version; it does not belong in version control.
#
# NOTE: 22 .pyc files committed by earlier cycles are still tracked. This file
# stops new ones appearing; removing the existing ones is a separate,
# deliberate change (`git rm -r --cached '**/__pycache__'`).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# pytest / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example